%2F49%2Fe1%2Ff426a1424cf28acecd6d3dcb0bb3%2Fap26329010191558.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5223x3482+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F49%2Fe1%2Ff426a1424cf28acecd6d3dcb0bb3%2Fap26329010191558.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5223x3482+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F49%2Fe1%2Ff426a1424cf28acecd6d3dcb0bb3%2Fap26329010191558.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5223x3482+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F49%2Fe1%2Ff426a1424cf28acecd6d3dcb0bb3%2Fap26329010191558.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5223x3482+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F49%2Fe1%2Ff426a1424cf28acecd6d3dcb0bb3%2Fap26329010191558.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5223x3482+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F49%2Fe1%2Ff426a1424cf28acecd6d3dcb0bb3%2Fap26329010191558.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5223x3482+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F49%2Fe1%2Ff426a1424cf28acecd6d3dcb0bb3%2Fap26329010191558.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5223x3482+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F49%2Fe1%2Ff426a1424cf28acecd6d3dcb0bb3%2Fap26329010191558.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5223x3482+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F49%2Fe1%2Ff426a1424cf28acecd6d3dcb0bb3%2Fap26329010191558.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5223x3482+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F49%2Fe1%2Ff426a1424cf28acecd6d3dcb0bb3%2Fap26329010191558.jpg" class="img" alt="Luke and Liam Laputka paddle their boat through floodwater caused by high tides, Tuesday, Nov. 24, 2026, in Sausalito, Calif." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Luke and Liam Laputka paddle their boat through floodwater caused by high tides, Tuesday, Nov. 24, 2026, in Sausalito, Calif.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Heather Diehl/AP                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;New York City's Central Park had its wettest Thanksgiving on record with 1.82 inches of rain. The city can expect strong winds on Friday, the weather service said, with gusts of up to 30 miles an hour.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Iconic Macy's parade postponed&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Macy's annual Thanksgiving Day Parade in the city has been postponed for the first time in its history and will now take place on Saturday. While it's never been postponed before, it was cancelled altogether for several years during World War II.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;aside id="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" class="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" aria-label="recommended stories"&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;    &lt;!-- END ID="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" CLASS="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" ARIA-LABEL="RECOMMENDED STORIES" --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Postponing it is causing major logistical problems, as there are around 11,000 participants in the parade, mostly volunteers, many of whom traveled in from out of state. But it's not safe to put up the iconic giant balloons the parade is known for during strong winds.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;There have been incidents where those balloons hurt people in past parades, most notably in 1997 when high winds caused a Cat in the Hat balloon to hit a lamp post and then strike a woman in the crowd, leaving her critically injured. Weather grounded all of the balloons for the parade only once, back in 1971.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Saturday's parade will be Macy's 100th. To mark the milestone there will be 100 balloons, Will Coss, the parade's executive producer, told NPR's Morning Edition's host A Martinez.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"Our first parade in 1924 had live animals. But the animals unfortunately scared the children a bit more than our early parade producers anticipated," Coss said, explaining that was when they brought in balloons.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"Each balloon has its own level of complexity so a balloon from 'beginning to end' can take anywhere from 4 to 6 months," said Coss, noting they are all first hand-drawn.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-156002" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 6784;         --source-height: 4523;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6784x4523+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff8%2Fb1%2F727579b84c02af97bfc70cdad9db%2Fap26330057499656.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6784x4523+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff8%2Fb1%2F727579b84c02af97bfc70cdad9db%2Fap26330057499656.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6784x4523+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff8%2Fb1%2F727579b84c02af97bfc70cdad9db%2Fap26330057499656.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6784x4523+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff8%2Fb1%2F727579b84c02af97bfc70cdad9db%2Fap26330057499656.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6784x4523+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff8%2Fb1%2F727579b84c02af97bfc70cdad9db%2Fap26330057499656.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6784x4523+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff8%2Fb1%2F727579b84c02af97bfc70cdad9db%2Fap26330057499656.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6784x4523+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff8%2Fb1%2F727579b84c02af97bfc70cdad9db%2Fap26330057499656.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6784x4523+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff8%2Fb1%2F727579b84c02af97bfc70cdad9db%2Fap26330057499656.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6784x4523+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff8%2Fb1%2F727579b84c02af97bfc70cdad9db%2Fap26330057499656.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6784x4523+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff8%2Fb1%2F727579b84c02af97bfc70cdad9db%2Fap26330057499656.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6784x4523+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff8%2Fb1%2F727579b84c02af97bfc70cdad9db%2Fap26330057499656.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6784x4523+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff8%2Fb1%2F727579b84c02af97bfc70cdad9db%2Fap26330057499656.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6784x4523+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff8%2Fb1%2F727579b84c02af97bfc70cdad9db%2Fap26330057499656.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6784x4523+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff8%2Fb1%2F727579b84c02af97bfc70cdad9db%2Fap26330057499656.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6784x4523+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff8%2Fb1%2F727579b84c02af97bfc70cdad9db%2Fap26330057499656.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6784x4523+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff8%2Fb1%2F727579b84c02af97bfc70cdad9db%2Fap26330057499656.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6784x4523+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff8%2Fb1%2F727579b84c02af97bfc70cdad9db%2Fap26330057499656.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6784x4523+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff8%2Fb1%2F727579b84c02af97bfc70cdad9db%2Fap26330057499656.jpg" class="img" alt="Workers deflate a balloon after the Macy&amp;#039;s Thanksgiving Day Parade was postponed Wednesday, Nov. 25, 2026, in New York." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Workers deflate a balloon after the Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade was postponed Wednesday, Nov. 25, 2026, in New York.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Yuki Iwamura/AP                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;This year there will be eight new giant balloons including Bluey, Hello Kitty and Mickey Mouse from the Sorcerer's Apprentice.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Returning favorites include Spongebob Squarepants, Spider-Man –– and the balloon that made its debut in 1927 as the parade's first inflated character: Felix The Cat.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Black Friday kicks off&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Americans are expected to spend more money today than on any other day of the year. But, amid inflation and high gas prices, a survey of almost 8,000 adult consumers found people are cutting back on other spending in order to prioritize expenses during the holiday season.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href="https://nrf.com/media-center/press-releases/183-million-consumers-expected-to-shop-during-thanksgiving-weekend" target="_blank"&gt;National Retail Federation&lt;/a&gt; expects some 183 million shoppers to spend over $1 trillion in November/December holiday sales. Many surveyed said the high cost of living would affect how they shopped, with some planning to buy less expensive gifts for fewer people.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;The majority of Americans would be shopping online, the Federation said, with 59% planning to use AI this year to help with recommendations, brainstorming gift ideas and scanning retailer sites to find the best prices.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;The organization said the top three children's toys this year are LEGO, Hot Wheels and Barbie dolls.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Kat Lonsdorf and Alina Selyukh in Washington DC and Kate Bartlett contributed to reporting.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
