r.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fde%2F2e%2F399887fb4ec881e2707d4ab12793%2Fd-d-lead-photo.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x2000+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fde%2F2e%2F399887fb4ec881e2707d4ab12793%2Fd-d-lead-photo.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x2000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fde%2F2e%2F399887fb4ec881e2707d4ab12793%2Fd-d-lead-photo.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x2000+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fde%2F2e%2F399887fb4ec881e2707d4ab12793%2Fd-d-lead-photo.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x2000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fde%2F2e%2F399887fb4ec881e2707d4ab12793%2Fd-d-lead-photo.jpg" class="img" alt="First published in 1974, Dungeons &amp;amp; Dragons is now being embraced by a new generation as a screen-free hobby." fetchpriority="high" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 First published in 1974, Dungeons &amp; Dragons is now being embraced by a new generation looking for a screen-free hobby.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Lauren Migaki/NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Dungeons &amp; Dragons has captivated players for more than 50 years.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;In its early days, some parents complained that the role-playing game kept kids holed up inside for hours at a time. NPR even did a 10-minute piece on it in 1979. &lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;More recently, D&amp;D has come back into popular culture &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/transcripts/1120523900" target="_blank"&gt;through shows including &lt;em&gt;Stranger Things&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, a &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2023/03/31/1166523475/dungeons-dragons-honor-among-thieves" target="_blank"&gt;2023 blockbuster movie&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://www.cnbc.com/2021/03/13/dungeons-dragons-had-its-biggest-year-despite-the-coronavirus.html" target="_blank"&gt;an influx of interest during the COVID-19 lockdowns&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Now, what was once a nerdy pastime has become a &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/05/01/nx-s1-5791657/states-schools-restricting-screen-time" target="_blank"&gt;screen-free parent's dream&lt;/a&gt; — a game that relies on imagination, a role of the dice and in-person communication.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;div id="resnx-s1-6042445-100" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col"&gt;                     &lt;!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" --&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;     &lt;!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-6042445-100" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;"It's a great concoction," Ted Fair says. He's the (grown-up) Dungeon Master for a group of 9- to 12-year-old kids in Washington Heights in New York. "When you're able to sit down with … other people and harmonize like that."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Fair's group is part of &lt;a href="https://tweenswithoutscreens.org/" target="_blank"&gt;Tweens Without Screens&lt;/a&gt;, a parent collective that focuses on providing technology-free activities for kids. They host events like knitting clubs and urban hikes. They have multiple D&amp;D groups that meet monthly.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-155245" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 2550;         --source-height: 3300;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2550x3300+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fe6%2Fa5%2Fcabe2f304ad9a833802c2741a3c9%2Fd-d-polaroid-01.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2550x3300+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fe6%2Fa5%2Fcabe2f304ad9a833802c2741a3c9%2Fd-d-polaroid-01.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2550x3300+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fe6%2Fa5%2Fcabe2f304ad9a833802c2741a3c9%2Fd-d-polaroid-01.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2550x3300+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fe6%2Fa5%2Fcabe2f304ad9a833802c2741a3c9%2Fd-d-polaroid-01.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2550x3300+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fe6%2Fa5%2Fcab