ps://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2550x3300+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fe6%2Fa5%2Fcabe2f304ad9a833802c2741a3c9%2Fd-d-polaroid-01.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2550x3300+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fe6%2Fa5%2Fcabe2f304ad9a833802c2741a3c9%2Fd-d-polaroid-01.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2550x3300+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fe6%2Fa5%2Fcabe2f304ad9a833802c2741a3c9%2Fd-d-polaroid-01.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2550x3300+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fe6%2Fa5%2Fcabe2f304ad9a833802c2741a3c9%2Fd-d-polaroid-01.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2550x3300+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fe6%2Fa5%2Fcabe2f304ad9a833802c2741a3c9%2Fd-d-polaroid-01.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2550x3300+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fe6%2Fa5%2Fcabe2f304ad9a833802c2741a3c9%2Fd-d-polaroid-01.jpg" class="img" alt="A polaroid photo of Rose Watson , her brother, Leo Watson, Amos Slodounik and Benjamin Cho. They are sitting on the floor after playing D&amp;amp;D. In front of them, character sheets, dice and a pad of paper with a hand-drawn map of their D&amp;amp;D world. Their group meets monthly and is hosted by Tweens Without Screens." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Rose Watson (left) with her brother, Leo Watson, Amos Slodounik and Benjamin Cho, are members of a D&amp;D group hosted by Tweens Without Screens                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Sequoia Carrillo/NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;"I feel like part of what's kind of fun about it is we're trying to figure it out as we go along," said Rose Watson, a 12-year-old member of Fair's D&amp;D crew.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resnx-s1-6042445-101" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col"&gt;                     &lt;!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" --&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;     &lt;!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-6042445-101" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;In their most recent session, the group explored a cave and discovered a mysterious egg. Possibly a dragon egg? They didn't get a chance to find out! A low roll of the dice meant that instead of successfully stealing the egg, it crashed into pieces on the floor.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"It's like painting a picture in your mind," said Watson. She likes the in-person nature of the game. "A big part of it is getting together with other people and friendship and making jokes."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"And collaboration!" added her 9-year-old brother Leo Watson.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="hr"&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/newsletter/ed" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Catch up on what you missed with our Education newsletter, sent weekly.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="hr"&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;       &lt;aside id="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" class="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" aria-label="recommended stories"&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;    &lt;!-- END ID="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" CLASS="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" ARIA-LABEL="RECOMMENDED STORIES" --&gt;    &lt;div id="resg-s1-155246" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 3000;         --source-height: 2000;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x2000+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fc3%2F63%2F0396b5ec4acc870916bc75948f49%2Fd-d-detail-photo.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x2000+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fc3%2F63%2F0396b5ec4acc870916bc75948f49%2Fd-d-detail-photo.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x2000+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fc3%2F63%2F0396b5ec4acc870916bc75948f49%2Fd-d-detail-photo.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x2000+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fc3%2F63%2F0396b5ec4acc870916bc75948f49%2Fd-d-detail-photo.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x2000+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fc3%2F63%2F0396b5ec4acc870916bc75948f49%2Fd-d-detail-photo.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x2000+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fc3%2F63%2F0396b5ec4acc870916bc75948f49%2Fd-d-detail-photo.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x2000+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fc3%2F63%2F0396b5ec4acc870916bc75948f49%2Fd-d-detail-photo.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x2000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fc3%2F63%2F0396b5ec4acc870916bc75948f49%2Fd-d-detail-photo.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x2000+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fc3%2F63%2F0396b5ec4acc870916bc75948f49%2Fd-d-detail-photo.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x2000+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fc3%2F63%2F0396b5ec4acc870916bc75948f49%2Fd-d-detail-photo.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x2000+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fc3%2F63%2F0396b5ec4acc870916bc75948f49%2Fd-d-detail-photo.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x2000+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fc3%2F63%2F0396b5ec4acc870916bc75948f49%2Fd-d-detail-photo.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x2000+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fc3%2F63%2F0396b5ec4acc870916bc75948f49%2Fd-d-detail-photo.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x2000+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fc3%2F63%2F0396b5ec4acc870916bc75948f49%2Fd-d-detail-photo.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x2000+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fc3%2F63%2F0396b5ec4acc870916bc75948f49%2Fd-d-detail-photo.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x2000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fc3%2F63%2F0396b5ec4acc870916bc75948f49%2Fd-d-detail-photo.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x2000+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fc3%2F63%2F0396b5ec4acc870916bc75948f49%2Fd-d-detail-photo.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x2000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fc3%2F63%2F0396b5ec4acc870916bc75948f49%2Fd-d-detail-photo.jpg" class="img" alt="Detail shot of one of the player&amp;#039;s character sheet next along with a physical book, opened to a page with drawings of weapons" loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 The players use pencils to fill out their character sheets and use books to look up questions about the game.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Lauren Migaki/NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;For fellow 9-year-old Amos Slodounik, it's about getting to try on a different personality.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"You can express yourself in different ways. You can be goofy and nobody will care," he said.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;And for Benjamin Cho, also 9, the fun is in the imagination. He spent much of the session drawing elaborate tools and creatures for their game (a healing spider donut, for example). "I like D&amp;D because there's a lot of items and things that you can make up."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/348774853/lauren-migaki" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lauren Migaki&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Audio story edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/348774853/lauren-migaki" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lauren Migaki&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;, &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/g-s1-123933/nirvi-shah" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Nirvi Shah&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; and &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/348780034/nicole-cohen" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Nicole Cohen&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Audio story produced by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/348774853/lauren-migaki" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lauren Migaki&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Visual design and development by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/348775569/la-johnson" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;LA Johnson&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
