webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F8a%2F7d%2F1a80d4454256a836e00a2981b1c7%2Fap26331031527493.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4053x2701+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F8a%2F7d%2F1a80d4454256a836e00a2981b1c7%2Fap26331031527493.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4053x2701+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F8a%2F7d%2F1a80d4454256a836e00a2981b1c7%2Fap26331031527493.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4053x2701+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F8a%2F7d%2F1a80d4454256a836e00a2981b1c7%2Fap26331031527493.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4053x2701+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F8a%2F7d%2F1a80d4454256a836e00a2981b1c7%2Fap26331031527493.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4053x2701+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F8a%2F7d%2F1a80d4454256a836e00a2981b1c7%2Fap26331031527493.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4053x2701+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F8a%2F7d%2F1a80d4454256a836e00a2981b1c7%2Fap26331031527493.jpg" class="img" alt="Philadelphia Eagles quarterback Joe Milton III (14) runs to score a touchdown against the Dallas Cowboys in the second half during an NFL football game in Arlington, Texas, Thursday, Nov. 26, 2026." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Philadelphia Eagles quarterback Joe Milton III (14) runs to score a touchdown against the Dallas Cowboys in the second half during an NFL football game in Arlington, Texas, Thursday, Nov. 26, 2026.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Julio Cortez/AP                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;"You never know when your opportunity is going to come. You never know, when, where, how. The only thing you can do is just prepare yourself," Milton said. "That's just the main thing I did. There wasn't a day where I was in a Cowboys facility and I didn't take notes. I didn't let a day go by where I didn't ask a question. So just being prepared for the moment and I mean, it showed up when it needed to. ... Really trying to hold my emotions in up here. Just thankful for the moment."&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;aside id="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" class="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" aria-label="recommended stories"&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;    &lt;!-- END ID="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" CLASS="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" ARIA-LABEL="RECOMMENDED STORIES" --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;While he was sacked five times, and the Cowboys defense had him on the run throughout, Milton made several big plays out of the pocket.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;On the 50-yard TD late in the first half, Milton rolled to his left and was in front of the Cowboys sideline when he threw back toward the center of the field — the ball was in the air more than 60 yards before Smith caught it at the goal line. Milton then looked toward the Dallas bench and made some seemingly good-natured gestures with a huge smile on his face.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"Can't even remember doing that, but it was just kind of in a moment," he said.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Then late in the third quarter, while rolling to his right toward his sideline, Milton threw deep to an open Smith, who after the catch had to take only a few steps into the end zone to complete the 45-yard score. Smith had 11 catches for 200 yards.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Milton's quick sprint down the sideline on his touchdown run got the Eagles within 38-30 with 9:09 left.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"He played his butt off. He played really good, made some throws that only he can make," coach Nick Sirianni said. "He played an outstanding game, super composed throughout."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;After appearing in four games for Dallas last season, Milton lost his backup role to Sam Howell in training camp this year. But Milton stayed with the Cowboys on their practice squad until getting signed by their NFC East rival.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-155995" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 4131;         --source-height: 2754;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4131x2754+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F0c%2Fca%2F8b9de7ee40ea992f176d896776b3%2Fap2