.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4131x2754+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F0c%2Fca%2F8b9de7ee40ea992f176d896776b3%2Fap26331070953822.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4131x2754+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F0c%2Fca%2F8b9de7ee40ea992f176d896776b3%2Fap26331070953822.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4131x2754+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F0c%2Fca%2F8b9de7ee40ea992f176d896776b3%2Fap26331070953822.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4131x2754+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F0c%2Fca%2F8b9de7ee40ea992f176d896776b3%2Fap26331070953822.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4131x2754+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F0c%2Fca%2F8b9de7ee40ea992f176d896776b3%2Fap26331070953822.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4131x2754+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F0c%2Fca%2F8b9de7ee40ea992f176d896776b3%2Fap26331070953822.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4131x2754+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F0c%2Fca%2F8b9de7ee40ea992f176d896776b3%2Fap26331070953822.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4131x2754+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F0c%2Fca%2F8b9de7ee40ea992f176d896776b3%2Fap26331070953822.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4131x2754+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F0c%2Fca%2F8b9de7ee40ea992f176d896776b3%2Fap26331070953822.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4131x2754+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F0c%2Fca%2F8b9de7ee40ea992f176d896776b3%2Fap26331070953822.jpg" class="img" alt="Dallas Cowboys quarterback Dak Prescott (4) embraces Philadelphia Eagles quarterback Joe Milton III (14) after an NFL football game in Arlington, Texas, Thursday, Nov. 26, 2026." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Dallas Cowboys quarterback Dak Prescott (4) embraces Philadelphia Eagles quarterback Joe Milton III (14) after an NFL football game in Arlington, Texas, Thursday, Nov. 26, 2026.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Julio Cortez/AP                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;The Eagles lost their seventh game in a row, 19-11 to the New York Giants in Milton's first start Nov. 8. After a bye week, they won 19-16 last Sunday over Pittsburgh, when Milton got them in range for a field goal and a two-score lead with four minutes remaining and then converted a third down in the final minute that allowed them to run out the clock.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;Only one of Milton's regular-season appearances for the Cowboys was at AT&amp;T Stadium, in a 34-17 loss to the Los Angeles Chargers last Dec. 21.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;His third start Thursday was only his eighth regular-season game in the NFL after appearing in nine preseason games — six for the Cowboys this season and last, along with three for New England in 2024 after the Patriots drafted him in the sixth round that year.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
